 r←PercentDecode r_;bad;n;hex;hv;pct;x2;xu;skip;p2;pu;cp;keep;len;bytes;c;success
⍝ Decodes percent-encoded text. "%XX" stands for a byte, and "%uXXXX" - not standard, but sent by
⍝ some clients - for a character. The bytes are taken to be UTF-8; wherever they are not valid
⍝ UTF-8, the offending sequence becomes U+FFFD, the replacement character, as the WHATWG URL
⍝ standard has it. So does a character that is not valid Unicode to begin with: a surrogate, or a
⍝ code point beyond U+10FFFF. No input whatsoever may cause an error: the data comes from the client.
⍝ A "%" that does not start an escape stays as it is, and so does every other character.
⍝ Decoding happens once: "%2541" becomes "%41", not "A".
⍝ "+" becomes a blank, as in query strings and form data; "%2B" is a "+".
⍝ The original Rumba function caused a LENGTH ERROR when the data contained both a blank and a
⍝ multi-byte character. Its replacement, taken from HttpCommands, decoded all escapes of the text
⍝ as one sequence of bytes - joining escapes that were not adjacent - and crashed the server with
⍝ a DOMAIN ERROR on invalid UTF-8 such as "/%C0".
 r←,r_
 ((r='+')/r)←' '
 cp←⎕UCS r
 bad←(cp>1114111)∨(55296≤cp)∧cp≤57343
 (bad/r)←⎕UCS 65533
 :If ∧/~pct←r='%'
     :Return
 :EndIf
 n←≢r
 hv←'0123456789ABCDEF0123456789abcdef'⍳r,5⍴'%'      ⍝ Padded: looking ahead never runs off the end
 hex←hv<32
 x2←pct∧(n↑1↓hex)∧n↑2↓hex                           ⍝ A "%XX" starts here
 cp←⎕UCS r
 :If ∨/'uU'∊r
     xu←pct∧(n↑1↓r,' ')∊'uU'
     xu∧←(n↑2↓hex)∧(n↑3↓hex)∧(n↑4↓hex)∧n↑5↓hex      ⍝ A "%uXXXX" starts here
⍝ The two cannot overlap: "u" is not a hex digit, and a hex digit is not a "%".
     skip←(n↑0,x2∨xu)∨(n↑0 0,x2∨xu)∨(n↑0 0 0,xu)∨(n↑0 0 0 0,xu)∨n↑0 0 0 0 0,xu ⍝ The rest of an escape
     pu←⍸xu
     cp[pu]←16⊥⍉16|hv[pu∘.+2+⍳4]
     cp[⍸(55296≤cp)∧cp≤57343]←65533                 ⍝ A lone surrogate is not a character
 :Else
     skip←(n↑0,x2)∨n↑0 0,x2
 :EndIf
 p2←⍸x2
 cp[p2]←0                                           ⍝ One byte, replaced below by the escaped one
 keep←~skip
 cp←keep/cp
 len←1+(cp≥128)+(cp≥2048)+cp≥65536                  ⍝ The length of every character in UTF-8
 bytes←'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⎕UCS cp
 bytes[(+\0,¯1↓len)[(+\keep)[p2]-1]]←16⊥⍉16|hv[p2∘.+1 2]
 :If ∧/bytes<128
     r←⎕UCS bytes
     :Return
 :EndIf
 success←0
 :Trap 11                                           ⍝ DOMAIN ERROR: the bytes are not valid UTF-8
⍝ `'UTF-8'⎕UCS` reads beyond the end of its argument: a sequence cut short by the end is completed
⍝ by whatever byte follows in memory, if that happens to be a continuation byte, instead of causing
⍝ a DOMAIN ERROR. The 0 cannot continue anything, so it makes the DOMAIN ERROR certain.
     r←¯1↓'UTF-8'⎕UCS bytes,0
     success←1
 :EndTrap
 :If success
     c←⎕UCS r                                       ⍝ ⎕UCS lets surrogates and code points beyond
     success←~∨/(c>1114111)∨(55296≤c)∧c≤57343       ⍝ U+10FFFF through rather than failing
 :EndIf
 :If ~success
     r←DecodeUTF8 bytes
 :EndIf
⍝Done
